From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 074/138] drm: adp: t7000: Stop the vram fetch when the CRTC is
 turned off

With the panel asleep the pipe still fetched a full 750x1334 XRGB frame
from vram at 60 Hz, which keeps the memory controller busy while the
screen is off.

With the new deep_off parameter (default off, writable at runtime), CRTC
off first does what iOS does first on display off
(AppleMobileADBE0::do_power_state_change_gated -> AppleH7DisplayPipe
"blank frame"): mask the non-vblank ADP interrupts and program a frame
with no layer (ADP 0x1038 = its bit 16 only, the value mainline
adp_drv.c also writes on plane disable), wait two frames for it to
latch, then put the panel to sleep as panel_sleep=1 does. CRTC on writes
the saved 0x1038 back, unmasks the interrupts it masked (after a W1C of
what latched meanwhile), waits two frames and wakes the panel. Base,
stride, format, blend, the timing generator and the DSI link are not
touched, so the undo is one register write.

iOS also stops the timing generator, the DSI link and the power domains
after the panel is off, but it never restarts the timings under a DSI
link left in video mode; that step is not known to be reversible here
and is left out.

Add a debugfs "power" file that runs the off/on sequence without DRM
master and shows the registers involved. deep_off=0 keeps the existing
panel_sleep behaviour.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adp/adp-t7000.c | 251 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
